01:03:21,680 --> 01:03:23,120
You may have been taught, how many vells

1359
01:03:23,120 --> 01:03:27,120
were you taught English had if you went to school in English?

1360
01:03:27,120 --> 01:03:28,120
Yeah?

1361
01:03:28,120 --> 01:03:28,620
Five.

1362
01:03:28,620 --> 01:03:29,120
Five.

1363
01:03:29,120 --> 01:03:30,160
It's supposed to have five, right?

1364
01:03:30,160 --> 01:03:31,040
It does not have five.

1365
01:03:31,040 --> 01:03:33,520
It has like 14.

1366
01:03:33,640 --> 01:03:37,720
And you know, why are we taught that it only has five?

1367
01:03:37,720 --> 01:03:40,280
Why do we only have five letters for vells?

1368
01:03:43,560 --> 01:03:46,080
Who gave us this alphabet?

1369
01:03:46,080 --> 01:03:47,840
The Romans, right?

1370
01:03:47,840 --> 01:03:48,480
Yeah?

1371
01:03:48,480 --> 01:03:50,880
And in Latin, there in fact are five vells, which

1372
01:03:50,880 --> 01:03:52,560
can be either long or short.

1373
01:03:52,560 --> 01:03:54,680
So this is a perfect alphabet for Latin.

1374
01:03:54,680 --> 01:03:55,180
Yeah?

1375
01:03:55,180 --> 01:03:57,040
But then we got hold of it.

1376
01:03:57,040 --> 01:04:01,880
And so we've ended up with 12, 14 vells, different dialects

1377
01:04:01,880 --> 01:04:03,440
of English or different.

1378
01:04:03,440 --> 01:04:05,680
And we have five letters to spell them with.

1379
01:04:05,680 --> 01:04:07,280
And this is why we have spelling Bs.

1380
01:04:07,280 --> 01:04:08,640
Yeah?

1381
01:04:08,640 --> 01:04:10,040
One of the reasons.

1382
01:04:10,040 --> 01:04:15,120
OK, so I've written six of our five vells here on this chart.

1383
01:04:15,120 --> 01:04:17,760
And then, but we have more.

1384
01:04:17,760 --> 01:04:21,400
So think about O and O, right?

1385
01:04:21,400 --> 01:04:29,640
In Houd and Hood, or E and E, and Heed and Hid, or A and E,

1386
01:04:29,680 --> 01:04:36,600
and Raid and Red, or O and A, like in coat and caught.

1387
01:04:36,600 --> 01:04:39,120
There are various ways of talking about this distinction.

1388
01:04:39,120 --> 01:04:41,120
But one way is like this.

1389
01:04:41,120 --> 01:04:42,880
We say that there's a distinction between what

1390
01:04:42,880 --> 01:04:46,800
are called tense vells and what are called lax vells.

1391
01:04:46,800 --> 01:04:52,920
So O is a high back rounded tense vowel.

1392
01:04:52,920 --> 01:04:55,760
And if you go back and forth between O and O,

1393
01:04:56,480 --> 01:05:03,640
O, O, O, the idea is basically what you're doing is relaxing.

1394
01:05:03,640 --> 01:05:07,680
So your tongue is not quite as rigidly high and back

1395
01:05:07,680 --> 01:05:10,480
as it would be for an O when it makes an O.

1396
01:05:10,480 --> 01:05:12,400
And your lips are probably not quite as

1397
01:05:12,400 --> 01:05:13,520
tensely rounded either.

1398
01:05:13,520 --> 01:05:16,720
Your whole body relaxes.

1399
01:05:16,720 --> 01:05:20,120
Same deal with all these other pairs.

1400
01:05:20,120 --> 01:05:22,400
It's a fact about English lax vowels

1401
01:05:22,400 --> 01:05:25,920
that there's a restriction on their distribution.

1402
01:05:25,920 --> 01:05:29,880
English monosyllables don't end in lax vells that

1403
01:05:29,880 --> 01:05:30,960
are either front or high.

1404
01:05:30,960 --> 01:05:35,320
So we have words like flea and flu and flay.

1405
01:05:35,320 --> 01:05:37,600
Those are all words in English.

1406
01:05:37,600 --> 01:05:41,040
Flay means to remove the skin from.

1407
